# Targeted per-file, per-rule exclusions. Deliberately NOT a global skip_list: the profile
# stays `production` and every other file is still held to it. Each entry below is a case
# where the rule is wrong for this repository, not a rule we could not be bothered to meet.

# ansible-vault ciphertext. The file IS the encrypted blob — there is no place to put a
# `---` document marker without corrupting it.
inventories/production/group_vars/all/vault.yml yaml[document-start]
inventories/staging/group_vars/all/vault.yml yaml[document-start]

# "Refresh APT cache after repository change" must run WHERE IT IS WRITTEN: it sits between
# adding the upstream repo and installing from it. A handler fires at the end of the play,
# so the install right below would run against a stale cache and pick the wrong version (or
# fail outright). The rule assumes a changed-when task is always deferrable; here it is not.
roles/caddy/tasks/main.yml no-handler
roles/docker/tasks/main.yml no-handler

# `system_users`, `greener_group` and `greener_shared_dir` are CROSS-ROLE by design:
# group_vars/all/users.yml is the single declarative source of accounts, and both `common`
# (system accounts) and `monitoring` (Grafana accounts) read it. Same for
# `grafana_user_passwords`, which comes from the vault indirection in group_vars, not from
# the role. The rule assumes role-private variables; prefixing these with `common_` or
# `monitoring_` would break that contract and lie about where they come from.
roles/common/defaults/main.yml var-naming[no-role-prefix]
roles/monitoring/defaults/main.yml var-naming[no-role-prefix]
